    "body": "# Description\r\n\r\nPlease include a brief summary of the changes, relevant motivation and context.\r\n\r\nThis change fixes an unintended behavior for EP-only workloads where GEMMs sharded like the following\r\n- activations: `[B(\"ep\"), S, H]`\r\n- weights: `[H, D(\"ep\")]`\r\nwill perform an all-gather on the activations. This is not desirable in the EP case as EP computation is intended to be FSDP-style outside of the expert layers, and as a result, we wouldn't expect an activation all-gather.\r\n\r\nAs a result, if a mesh axis shards both a non-contracting dim of the activations and a non-contracting dim of the weights, we now gather the weights along that axis (as is already done for FSDP). Only the overlapping axes are dropped from compound weight specs, e.g. `(\"ep\", \"tp\")` -> `\"tp\"`.\r\n\r\nWe make an exception for TPSP workloads, since there we expect activations to be gathered on the sequence dimension; TP and TPSP axes are therefore ignored in this gather.\r\n\r\nWe additionally add tests validating the EP-only behavior, compound weight specs, and that existing TP/TPSP (including collective GEMM) sharding is unchanged.\r\n\r\nFixes # (issue)\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n\r\n- [ ] Documentation change (change only to the documentation, either a fix or a new content)\r\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n- [ ] Infra/Build change\r\n- [ ] Code refactoring\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Fix sharding spec removal so that EP-only workloads have weights gathered instead of activations. Additionally, allow only overlapping axes to be dropped from weight specs.\r\n- Add tests to validate behavior.\r\n\r\n# Checklist:\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\r\n- [x] The functionality is complete\r\n- [x] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\r\n- [x] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\r\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings\r\n- [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works\r\n- [x] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\r\n",
