      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=82411879\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/nvidia-public-github/github/NVIDIA/transformerengine/-/pull/3697\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptileDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptile.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"View in Greptile\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewInGreptile.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 4/5</h2>\n\n**[High impact]** Changes core GEMM sharding logic for distributed training\\.\n\nFix compound activation sharding before merging; the new weight behavior can produce an invalid output spec.\n\n<h2>Findings</h2>\n\n1. <img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Compound sharding repeats an axis** <a href=\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/3697#discussion_r4297983244\">▶</a>\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nThis PR gathers weights rather than activations when EP shares an axis across both operands.\n- Plain GEMMs gather shared EP weight axes and keep activations sharded.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:4 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Fix EP-only sharding gather logic so jus...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/59a8dbdbcc422a6206a3128a0ce4a0d2c3a6f16a) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_review&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=review_public&utm_content=nvidia/transformerengine)</sub>",
